 "defect_observations": [
  "handbook/parts/p02/variants.tex 33-40 (read-only host) still says the reduction needs Sort, F, R at most countable and that larger signatures 'are not in the scope of that theorem'. After routing this is superseded for F and R by thm:p02-w02b-p02-033-variable-form and for Sort by thm:p02-w02b-p02-033-reduction, but variants.tex has no forward pointer (the editable host w02-p02-038 body 42-52 has one). The lead should reconcile it.",
  "handbook/annex/p02/higher-order-supplement.tex 22-60 (annex:p2.hol.5) is a sketch ('The same induction gives truth preservation'). The written proofs are in the w02-p02-038 annex 347-433 and the owned annex 122-362.",
  "handbook/parts/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02-p02-038.tex 58-59 defines FV only 'by the usual recursion'. FV is not a listed component.",
  "Owned body 399-400 says an injective renaming exists exactly when Var_MS is countable, with no written proof of the 'if' direction (it follows at once from the definition of countable).",
  "w02-p02-038 body 602-604 (empty-sort comparison, clause 4) still fixes an injection of an at most countable symbol set. This is outside the strict-convention scope of D-P3-007, and owned body 490-493 acknowledges it.",
  "Owned body 510-523 cites Pitts1995Draft at page locators for a contextual remark. That is not a component requirement; the locators were not opened (S6 does not apply).",
  "unit-compile reported 12 overfull boxes (typesetting only)."
